# drexbot-shop.env.example: the settings drexbot-shop.service reads.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/drexbot/shop.env and edit. Every value here is invented.
# systemd reads one VAR=value per line and does not expand anything in it.
#
# The store must also be listed in ~/.config/drexbot/swarm-targets, and a
# baseline captured for --env, as for any `swarm run`.

# The flags for `drexbot swarm shop`, on one line. --night is the local-time
# window that holds the daily deploy, and may cross midnight; 25 orders every
# slice inside it, 5 outside it, unless --night-orders and --day-orders say
# otherwise. Add --seconds 240 to load for less than the whole five minutes, so
# the bees are removed before the next tick finds the service still running.
DREXBOT_SHOP_FLAGS=--url http://shop.example.com:8080 --env showcase --night 01:00-05:00 --sku EXAMPLE-SKU-1 --network showcase_default --mix normal-day

# Orders are placed, which nothing here can take back: set this only for a
# store you would not mind finding test orders in.
MAGENTO_DISPOSABLE=1
